make changes in the www directory; commit and push

sign into AWS, navigate to S3, and then the bucket named www.willowbench.bio

(for each directory that has changed/new files)
  navigate to the directory
  click upload
  drag and drop any changed or new files in that directory
    *IMPORTANT*: if you upload an HTML file with no extension, e.g. "about", "contact", then:
    expand the "Properties" menu at the bottom of the upload page
    click "Add metadata" at the bottom
    type "System defined", Key "Content-Type", Value "text/html" (text/html won't be a suggestion, but it's correct)


navigate to AWS Cloudfront. select what should be the only "Distribution" (its ID is E14LG3CWMWUJLY in case there are others)

go to the Invalidations tab, and "Create invalidation"

add object paths as instructed. e.g.
/index.html
/about
/images/casey.jpg


then click "create invalidation"

wait until the invalidation status moves on from "In progress" to "Completed", wait another several seconds, then visit willowbench.bio in incognito to check that the changes are live.
